WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.286
In a moment you'll build your first hànzì. Before that, let me show you why building is the right way to learn them.

2
00:00:08.286 --> 00:00:17.929
木 is tree: a trunk down the middle, branches opening out. 人 is person: two strokes leaning on each other. Hold on to both for a moment.

3
00:00:17.929 --> 00:00:25.143
On the left, 人, person. On the right, 木, tree. Together they form 休: a person beside a tree, resting.

4
00:00:25.143 --> 00:00:41.357
You read a new character by spotting two shapes you had just seen. That is how Chinese writing stops being thousands of separate drawings and becomes a system. You don't need to memorise 休 — you need to notice this is possible.

5
00:00:41.357 --> 00:00:43.557
This is not scored.

6
00:00:43.557 --> 00:00:52.629
In the builder you'll fit the parts of each character together. It isn't calligraphy: it's noticing what each hànzì is made of.
